{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-26601","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31377","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31378","text":"The road as a windowing system — half of "},{"id":"spn-31379","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R (Travel & RRABBIT)"},{"id":"spn-31380","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26603","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31381","marks":["bold"],"text":"Travel and RRABBIT are two personalities, not two layers."},{"id":"spn-31382","text":" Travel wants to navigate: the road, the camera, the flight into a window, the districts. RRABBIT wants to "},{"id":"spn-31383","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-31384","text":" the windows — the sign standing on the road, the surface that flattens to 1:1 under you, the rect that decides a click is yours. One likes going; the other likes being gone to."}]},{"id":"blk-26604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31385","text":"This repo is a fork of "},{"id":"spn-31386","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-31387","text":"'s world, re-missioned from "},{"id":"spn-31388","marks":["italic"],"text":"rendering a build harness"},{"id":"spn-31389","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-31390","marks":["italic"],"text":"managing an operating system's windows"},{"id":"spn-31391","text":", and it holds both of them — as two modules rather than one file:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26606","spans":[{"id":"spn-31392","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-26607","spans":[{"id":"spn-31393","text":"who"}]},{"id":"blk-26608","spans":[{"id":"spn-31394","text":"what is in it"}]}],"id":"blk-26605","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26609","spans":[{"id":"spn-31395","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/travel.js"}],"text":"`m2/travel.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26610","spans":[{"id":"spn-31396","text":"Travel"}]},{"id":"blk-26611","spans":[{"id":"spn-31397","text":"poses, districts, overview, the flatten, the flight, input routing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26612","spans":[{"id":"spn-31398","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/rrabbit.js"}],"text":"`m2/rrabbit.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26613","spans":[{"id":"spn-31399","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26614","spans":[{"id":"spn-31400","text":"texture adoption, signs, popups, the ledger rect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26615","spans":[{"id":"spn-31401","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/world.js"}],"text":"`m2/world.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26616","spans":[{"id":"spn-31402","text":"neither"}]},{"id":"blk-26617","spans":[{"id":"spn-31403","text":"the stage: scene handles, the "},{"id":"spn-31404","marks":["code"],"text":"signs"},{"id":"spn-31405","text":" ledger, the numbers the HUD reads"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26618","spans":[{"id":"spn-31406","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/shell.js"}],"text":"`m2/shell.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26619","spans":[{"id":"spn-31407","text":"the wiring"}]},{"id":"blk-26620","spans":[{"id":"spn-31408","text":"builds the world, drives the frame, owns the diagnostics"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26621","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31409","text":"They say very little to each other. Travel reads two things and both come through the shared ledger rather than a call — which sign stands at an address, and what rect it owns in the flat output. RRABBIT calls Travel "},{"id":"spn-31410","marks":["bold"],"text":"once"},{"id":"spn-31411","text":": when a window dies while you are standing in it, it tells Travel to let go. That is the whole conversation, and it runs in one direction."}]},{"id":"blk-26622","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31412","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/travel-and-rrabbit"}],"text":"travel-and-rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-31413","text":" is the distribution — it carries Travel's name and is not Travel either."}]},{"id":"blk-26623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31414","text":"Signs on the road are no longer journal rows. "},{"id":"spn-31415","marks":["bold"],"text":"They are the running applications."},{"id":"spn-31416","text":" The vacuum tubes are no longer lane ratings; they are CPU, RAM, swap, disk, net, temp and load. Districts are no longer amp workspaces; they are desktop workspaces. You drive past your windows, fly into one, and it flattens into a real, square, pixel-exact surface you can type into."}]},{"id":"blk-26624","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31417","text":"It shows only windows launched into it. It does not replace your desktop."}]},{"id":"blk-26625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31418","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read [`docs/spec/README.md`](docs/spec/README.md) first"},{"id":"spn-31419","text":" — in particular §2, which records what does "},{"id":"spn-31420","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-31421","text":" work about the obvious integration and why."}]},{"id":"blk-26626","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31422","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-26627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31423","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0–M5 built, M0–M4 measured"},{"id":"spn-31424","text":" (2026-08-08), each with measurements rather than screenshots alone — spec §10–§12 and §14–§17. "},{"id":"spn-31425","marks":["bold"],"text":"Booted on T&R 2026-08-09."}]},{"id":"blk-26628","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31426","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0"},{"id":"spn-31427","text":" — the road occludes a live Wayland surface. This was the gate."}]}],"id":"blk-26629","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26632","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31428","marks":["bold"],"text":"M1"},{"id":"spn-31429","text":" — many windows ride the road as signs, one adopted GPU texture each,"}]}],"id":"blk-26631","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26633","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31430","text":"at stable milepost addresses. No Greenfield patch was needed after all (§11.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-26634","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31431","marks":["bold"],"text":"M2"},{"id":"spn-31432","text":" — flying into a sign arrives fronto-parallel at exactly 1:1, where it"}]}],"id":"blk-26635","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26637","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31433","text":"can be pointed at, typed into, and left with a chord no client can swallow."}]},{"id":"blk-26638","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31434","marks":["bold"],"text":"M3"},{"id":"spn-31435","text":" — seven tubes reading the real machine, and a rack that is not allowed"}]}],"id":"blk-26639","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26641","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31436","text":"to show a number it cannot explain."}]},{"id":"blk-26642","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31437","marks":["bold"],"text":"M4"},{"id":"spn-31438","text":" — three districts as workspaces, each a road of its own, and a ledger"}]}],"id":"blk-26643","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26645","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31439","text":"where every window has its own rect so input resolves by position (§15.2)."}]},{"id":"blk-26646","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26648","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31440","marks":["bold"],"text":"popups"},{"id":"spn-31441","text":" — §7's open problem, closed (§16). Also found that an "},{"id":"spn-31442","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"}]}],"id":"blk-26647","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31443","text":"cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26650","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31444","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-31445","text":" — runs as a session: Python-only on the target, and Firefox runs the"}]}],"id":"blk-26651","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31446","text":"whole shell."}]},{"id":"blk-26654","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31447","marks":["bold"],"text":"BOOT"},{"id":"spn-31448","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-31449","marks":["bold"],"text":"runs on a T&R image"},{"id":"spn-31450","text":" (2026-08-09). Greeter to road on the"}]}],"id":"blk-26655","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31451","text":"distribution it is built for, in a 4 GB guest with no GPU. Six of seven tubes read the real FreeBSD machine; "},{"id":"spn-31452","marks":["code"],"text":"temp"},{"id":"spn-31453","text":" reports its own absence, because a VM has no "},{"id":"spn-31454","marks":["code"],"text":"dev.cpu.0.temperature"},{"id":"spn-31455","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31456","text":"Three things that only a real boot could have found, all now fixed:"}]},{"id":"blk-26659","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26661","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31457","marks":["bold"],"text":"`make.sh` could not carry the shell to the builder at all."},{"id":"spn-31458","text":" "},{"id":"spn-31459","marks":["code"],"text":"build-image.sh"}]}],"id":"blk-26660","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31460","text":"reads "},{"id":"spn-31461","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_DIST"},{"id":"spn-31462","text":" as a path on the machine doing the build, and that machine is never the workstation — so there was no route from a built bundle to an image. It pushes "},{"id":"spn-31463","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-31464","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-31465","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-31466","text":" now, and refuses a "},{"id":"spn-31467","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-31468","text":" older than its sources."}]},{"id":"blk-26663","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26665","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31469","marks":["bold"],"text":"The FreeBSD tube reader had never executed."},{"id":"spn-31470","text":" "},{"id":"spn-31471","marks":["code"],"text":"net"},{"id":"spn-31472","text":" raised "},{"id":"spn-31473","marks":["code"],"text":"TypeError"},{"id":"spn-31474","text":" on a"}]}],"id":"blk-26664","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31475","marks":["code"],"text":"None"},{"id":"spn-31476","text":" peak the first time it ran. Fixed by giving it the same prior-peak protocol "},{"id":"spn-31477","marks":["code"],"text":"LinuxReader"},{"id":"spn-31478","text":" already had — patching only the crash would have re-introduced the bug that note describes, where the first byte pins the gauge at 100%."}]},{"id":"blk-26667","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26669","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31479","marks":["bold"],"text":"The greeter preselected RRABBIT, and could not select anything else."},{"id":"spn-31480","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26668","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31481","marks":["code"],"text":".desktop"},{"id":"spn-31482","text":" entries, picked by sort order, and "},{"id":"spn-31483","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-31484","text":" sorts before "},{"id":"spn-31485","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr"},{"id":"spn-31486","text":" — so a fresh image logged into the 3D shell, which is precisely what "},{"id":"spn-31487","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-31488","text":" says must never happen. The session label was blank as well: it asked SDDM's "},{"id":"spn-31489","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionModel"},{"id":"spn-31490","text":" for "},{"id":"spn-31491","marks":["code"],"text":"Qt.DisplayRole"},{"id":"spn-31492","text":", which that model does not publish. T&R now seeds the default and the greeter takes "},{"id":"spn-31493","marks":["bold"],"text":"F2"},{"id":"spn-31494","text":" to change it."}]},{"id":"blk-26671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31495","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native applications work"},{"id":"spn-31496","text":" (§18). A real "},{"id":"spn-31497","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-31498","text":" runs on the road — X11 → XWayland → nested compositor → h264 → browser → GPU texture → sign — flattened to "},{"id":"spn-31499","marks":["bold"],"text":"960×653 at `scale 1.0000`"},{"id":"spn-31500","text":", prompt legible. §13 spent its whole length searching the environment and the cause was not in the environment: the official addon build "},{"id":"spn-31501","marks":["bold"],"text":"compiles its own GStreamer at branch 1.20"},{"id":"spn-31502","text":" and this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-31503","marks":["bold"],"text":"1.28.6"},{"id":"spn-31504","text":", so the shipped "},{"id":"spn-31505","marks":["code"],"text":"libproxy-encoding.so"},{"id":"spn-31506","text":" linked a GStreamer GL that was not the installed one. Every symbol resolved the entire time it was silently emitting nothing — "},{"id":"spn-31507","marks":["code"],"text":"ldd"},{"id":"spn-31508","text":" resolving is not evidence a native module matches its dependencies. The rebuild is now "},{"id":"spn-31509","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run addons"},{"id":"spn-31510","text":", pinned and hash-checked (§19)."}]},{"id":"blk-26672","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31511","text":"Still true, and not smoothed over:"}]},{"id":"blk-26673","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31512","marks":["bold"],"text":"Frames tear — two thirds fixed, and the rest now measured"},{"id":"spn-31513","text":" (§20). It was"}]}],"id":"blk-26674","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26676","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31514","text":"never a damage-region problem. three left a "},{"id":"spn-31515","marks":["bold"],"text":"vertex array bound"},{"id":"spn-31516","text":" and Greenfield's YUV→RGB pass binds none of its own, so it recorded its attribute pointers into three's VAO and drew with three's leftovers; that was the full-canvas magnified-glyph artifact, and it is gone. Separately the decoded texture is "},{"id":"spn-31517","marks":["bold"],"text":"larger than the surface"},{"id":"spn-31518","text":" — 1024×770 for a 960×653 xterm — and the sign was mapping the padding too; it now samples the same sub-rect Greenfield's own shader does. What remains is a constant-slope diagonal with flat cyan below it, inside the decoded content: chroma left at default, so never written. That is upstream in "},{"id":"spn-31519","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-31520","text":", and the encoder A/B that would narrow it could not be run — see §20.3."}]},{"id":"blk-26677","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26679","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31521","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-window encode cost is still unpriced, and §21.2 says why."},{"id":"spn-31522","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26678","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31523","text":"harnesses, neither monotonic in window count. What they did establish: the proxy is flat at ~0.4% CPU while the browser sits at 425%, so the expensive half is decode and composite, not encode — \"per-window encode cost\" may be the wrong first question."}]},{"id":"blk-26681","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26683","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31524","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native launches drop above two"},{"id":"spn-31525","text":" (§21.3). Ask for four windows, get two,"}]}],"id":"blk-26682","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31526","text":"with nothing reported. Found while measuring something else, not diagnosed. The multi-window case is not just unpriced, it is unreliable."}]},{"id":"blk-26685","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31527","marks":["bold"],"text":"Signs carry no titles yet."}]}],"id":"blk-26686","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31528","text":"Closed since: a "},{"id":"spn-31529","marks":["bold"],"text":"reload no longer strands the remote client"},{"id":"spn-31530","text":" (§21.1) — each page load takes a fresh session id and "},{"id":"spn-31531","marks":["code"],"text":"pagehide"},{"id":"spn-31532","text":" reaps the old one, verified across three reloads against a proxy that was never restarted, leaving exactly one "},{"id":"spn-31533","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-31534","text":" behind."}]},{"id":"blk-26689","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31535","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-31536","text":" is no longer on this list — §16 closed it, and found on the way that a popup cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26690","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31537","text":"Local patches — do not lose these"}]},{"id":"blk-26691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31538","text":"RRABBIT carries a "},{"id":"spn-31539","marks":["bold"],"text":"required"},{"id":"spn-31540","text":" one-line fix to "},{"id":"spn-31541","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-31542","text":": without it an "},{"id":"spn-31543","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-31544","text":" can never map, so "},{"id":"spn-31545","marks":["bold"],"text":"no client can show a menu, dropdown or tooltip"},{"id":"spn-31546","text":". "},{"id":"spn-31547","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules/"},{"id":"spn-31548","text":" is gitignored, so the fix lives in "},{"id":"spn-31549","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/"}],"text":"`patches/`"},{"id":"spn-31550","text":" and is re-applied by "},{"id":"spn-31551","marks":["code"],"text":"postinstall"},{"id":"spn-31552","text":" and by "},{"id":"spn-31553","marks":["code"],"text":"build"},{"id":"spn-31554","text":". A runtime detector warns if it is ever missing rather than silently repairing it."}]},{"id":"blk-26692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31555","text":"Read "},{"id":"spn-31556","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/README.md"}],"text":"`patches/README.md`"},{"id":"spn-31557","text":" before touching "},{"id":"spn-31558","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-31559","text":" scripts or upgrading "},{"id":"spn-31560","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-31561","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26693","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31562","text":"Lineage"}]},{"id":"blk-26694","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26696","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31563","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-31564","text":" — the world this forks, and the source of every measured"}]}],"id":"blk-26695","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26697","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31565","text":"constant ("},{"id":"spn-31566","marks":["code"],"text":"S"},{"id":"spn-31567","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31568","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOST_X"},{"id":"spn-31569","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31570","marks":["code"],"text":"MIR_TILT"},{"id":"spn-31571","text":", the hood clip, the yoke camera framing)"}]},{"id":"blk-26698","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26700","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31572","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/PARKVPS"}],"text":"PARKVPS"},{"id":"spn-31573","text":" — the fleet whose rail proved"}]}],"id":"blk-26699","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26701","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31574","text":"the tab strip shape, and the origin of the "},{"id":"spn-31575","marks":["code"],"text":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Esc"},{"id":"spn-31576","text":" escape hatch"}]},{"id":"blk-26702","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26704","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31577","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/udevbe/greenfield"}],"text":"Greenfield"},{"id":"spn-31578","text":" — the in-browser Wayland"}]}],"id":"blk-26703","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26705","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31579","text":"compositor, AGPL-3.0"}]},{"id":"blk-26706","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26708","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31580","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://www.collabora.com/news-and-blog/news-and-events/wxrd-a-standalone-wayland-compositor-for-xrdesktop.html"}],"text":"wxrd"}]}],"id":"blk-26707","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26709","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31581","text":"/ "},{"id":"spn-31582","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/evil0sheep/motorcar"}],"text":"motorcar"},{"id":"spn-31583","text":" — the 3D-windowing prior art, and where the scoping decision comes from"}]},{"id":"blk-26710","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31584","text":"Licence"}]},{"id":"blk-26711","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31585","text":"AGPL-3.0, inherited from Greenfield. See spec §9."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawcbe2725ymkxpaouq2ffi3a3zkduumrfbafpfebn4fzxxwf2oycq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}